WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.220
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.860 --> 01:15.060
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.000 --> 01:21.560
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.340 --> 01:24.070
...is often called this...

01:24.140 --> 01:29.880
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:32.550 --> 01:33.780
Oh...

01:33.850 --> 01:36.320
I see it. The demon's powers...

01:36.390 --> 01:38.320
I can see it!

01:56.740 --> 01:59.180
This is the end of the first act.

02:05.180 --> 02:06.050
Brother!

02:07.390 --> 02:08.980
Brother, this is bad.

02:09.050 --> 02:10.450
The research lab...

02:10.990 --> 02:13.020
The research lab is on fire.

02:13.460 --> 02:17.520
Mr. Mikuriya is seeking our help!

02:26.170 --> 02:27.470
<i>Confinement</i>

02:27.470 --> 02:31.310
<i>Confinement
Episode 14</i>

02:59.140 --> 03:00.110
Naoya...

03:01.510 --> 03:03.480
Regardless of how
the real world changes...

03:03.540 --> 03:05.640
...there is no mistake
to our memories.

03:06.080 --> 03:08.050
I know, Brother.

03:16.290 --> 03:18.260
Naoto, come out.

03:18.720 --> 03:20.990
How long are you
going to stay in there?

03:21.060 --> 03:22.150
Shut up!

03:23.230 --> 03:27.790
If you promise that you will let us
go home, then we'll come out!

03:27.970 --> 03:29.260
Naoto...

03:34.070 --> 03:38.480
If you want us to come out of here,
then bring Mom and Dad here!

03:38.540 --> 03:42.070
Until then, we will never come out!

03:48.290 --> 03:49.450
Damn it...

04:08.810 --> 04:12.070
If you don't eat a little bit,
you aren't going to last.

04:12.950 --> 04:15.380
I'm going to leave your meal here.

04:18.480 --> 04:20.950
I beg you, please eat it, okay?

04:21.020 --> 04:23.580
If Mom and Dad don't come,
we won't eat!

04:25.860 --> 04:27.090
Poor things...

05:21.210 --> 05:25.510
Mr. Mikuriya isn't here today,
so let's play outside.

05:25.880 --> 05:29.010
It's too boring if it's always
inside the house, right?

05:34.030 --> 05:35.580
It ate my treat.

05:35.660 --> 05:37.860
Good job, Naoya!

05:38.100 --> 05:39.090
Yeah!

05:39.230 --> 05:42.720
They have been
living here for a while.

05:43.000 --> 05:46.460
They're used to people, so even if
you touch them, they don't run away.

05:46.640 --> 05:48.270
Aren't they cute?

05:51.840 --> 05:53.610
Hey, wait!

05:54.910 --> 05:58.180
If we come out of that room,
what's going to happen?

05:59.020 --> 06:01.610
Mr. Mikuriya will teach you.

06:02.450 --> 06:07.410
Many things which you
wouldn't learn in a normal school.

06:08.160 --> 06:09.320
Brother!

06:09.500 --> 06:10.690
Look!

06:11.660 --> 06:13.320
See? I was able to hold it!

06:13.400 --> 06:14.760
I was able to hold it!

06:14.830 --> 06:16.560
Amazing!

06:17.070 --> 06:19.830
Mr. Naoya, that's amazing.

06:24.080 --> 06:25.480
Mr. Naoya!

06:35.320 --> 06:37.020
These kids are scary.

06:37.090 --> 06:38.490
They creep me out.

06:38.690 --> 06:41.450
I don't want them to
do something to me, but...

06:41.530 --> 06:43.790
But this is for money.

06:44.660 --> 06:46.130
I have to deal with it.

06:46.200 --> 06:48.930
As long as I don't get hurt,
I can do something about it.

06:49.000 --> 06:49.970
Deal with it.

06:52.340 --> 06:53.330
Naoya!

06:55.810 --> 06:57.240
Naoya! Get it together!

06:57.410 --> 06:58.100
Naoya!

07:08.850 --> 07:09.840
Brother...

07:13.630 --> 07:17.120
Mr. Mikuriya is watching us.

07:18.360 --> 07:22.700
This lady was forced
to be with us for money.

07:22.940 --> 07:23.990
Help...

07:24.140 --> 07:25.360
Help me...

07:34.050 --> 07:35.310
Damn it...

07:35.750 --> 07:36.770
Naoya, come!

07:52.200 --> 07:54.600
The rope is still here...

07:59.510 --> 08:00.490
Damn it!

08:09.920 --> 08:11.780
Definitely not going back.

08:12.180 --> 08:14.580
We are definitely
not going back there.

08:15.490 --> 08:16.350
Yeah.

08:29.200 --> 08:30.290
Brother...

08:46.420 --> 08:47.910
You can't get out?

08:55.560 --> 08:56.890
It's mysterious.

08:57.130 --> 08:58.820
I can't touch it.

09:02.430 --> 09:05.370
Does that mean
it's filtering you two?

09:08.010 --> 09:11.460
That woman is a normal person.

09:12.340 --> 09:16.440
It's a natural thing
to work for money.

09:17.780 --> 09:19.340
How impressive.

09:19.890 --> 09:21.510
You started the fire yourself?

09:23.460 --> 09:25.450
There is no power
that has no meaning.

09:26.360 --> 09:30.820
There is definitely a meaning
for your powers.

09:31.800 --> 09:34.730
I will definitely save you two.

09:34.800 --> 09:36.830
You won't be able to do it.

09:38.440 --> 09:39.900
There's no way you can do it.

09:40.910 --> 09:41.900
I beg you...

09:42.640 --> 09:43.840
Please stay here.

09:47.050 --> 09:47.980
Let's go back.

09:48.850 --> 09:49.910
Come on.

10:08.730 --> 10:09.720
Naoya...

10:15.840 --> 10:18.210
I'm an ally.

10:20.410 --> 10:22.070
I'm an ally.

10:42.600 --> 10:43.970
It's magnetism.

10:44.970 --> 10:45.900
Yeah.

11:54.670 --> 11:55.730
That night...

11:56.410 --> 11:59.640
...I thought of giving up getting
out of there for a split second.

11:59.710 --> 12:00.510
What?

12:14.630 --> 12:16.290
Yes! I've passed it!

12:17.230 --> 12:18.390
I passed it!

12:20.630 --> 12:22.360
Naoya, come on, jump!

12:22.430 --> 12:23.400
Jump!

12:24.140 --> 12:25.540
Brother...

12:26.810 --> 12:29.100
You were scared...

12:29.640 --> 12:34.040
I thought it might be impossible
to take you with me.

12:34.580 --> 12:37.910
But, it was good I got to go outside.

12:38.320 --> 12:39.370
Yeah.

12:39.620 --> 12:42.020
It was good I got to
get outside with you.

12:43.660 --> 12:45.590
If I wasn't with you...

12:46.590 --> 12:49.920
...I don't know what
would have happened to me.

13:00.740 --> 13:01.930
It's too late!

13:02.210 --> 13:04.470
The research lab has burned down!

13:04.540 --> 13:05.200
What?

13:16.760 --> 13:18.660
So I was right...

13:18.920 --> 13:22.860
The barrier that Elder Misaki made
was protecting this place.

13:23.230 --> 13:24.220
What...

13:24.900 --> 13:26.260
What happened?

13:26.970 --> 13:28.060
Where's Mikuriya?

13:28.330 --> 13:29.060
Where's Mariko?

13:43.650 --> 13:44.640
I see...

13:45.380 --> 13:46.980
I see it, Brother.

13:47.720 --> 13:49.210
So many of them came here.

13:49.550 --> 13:50.540
At night!

13:50.620 --> 13:53.090
They are carrying documents out
one after another!

13:54.760 --> 13:59.360
Mr. Mikuriya is just quietly watching
without saying anything.

14:00.700 --> 14:03.500
He already knows that it's the end.

14:06.740 --> 14:07.710
The fire!

14:07.770 --> 14:09.800
They are setting the building on fire!

14:10.010 --> 14:11.270
This is horrible...

14:12.610 --> 14:15.100
Where did everyone go?

14:15.680 --> 14:17.050
I don't know.

14:20.390 --> 14:21.610
Three of them!

14:21.690 --> 14:22.680
I'm scared!

14:22.750 --> 14:24.310
What happened to Mikuriya!

14:24.560 --> 14:25.890
By the woman...

14:33.370 --> 14:34.420
What happened!

14:36.900 --> 14:39.700
No. He was almost killed when
the woman went on a rampage...

14:39.770 --> 14:42.640
...but her comrades stopped her.

14:43.740 --> 14:45.040
Is he still alive then?

14:48.050 --> 14:49.070
Mr. Mikuriya is...

14:52.220 --> 14:54.950
Mr. Mikuriya is still alive.

15:13.070 --> 15:14.270
Here they are.

15:17.910 --> 15:19.310
You guys seem well.

15:28.320 --> 15:29.750
Well, sit down.

15:30.990 --> 15:32.180
What happened?

15:32.320 --> 15:33.720
Where are the researchers?

15:34.130 --> 15:35.060
Where is Mariko?

15:35.130 --> 15:37.090
They were all taken away.

15:37.700 --> 15:39.790
I saw Masayuki and his mother.

15:40.130 --> 15:41.060
Sonezaki too.

15:44.370 --> 15:45.530
Is that so?

15:46.100 --> 15:47.870
You saw Sonezaki?

15:48.570 --> 15:49.510
Yeah.

15:49.670 --> 15:54.270
I didn't think that he would
become part of their group too.

15:55.080 --> 15:58.380
That's because Sonezaki
wasn't the type to be in a big crowd...

15:59.250 --> 16:02.950
But I guess he
might have been lonely.

16:06.020 --> 16:07.960
Let's make this end here.

16:10.160 --> 16:13.130
Let's make your
lonesome suffering end here.

16:17.000 --> 16:19.370
He was lonely for a very long time.

16:20.070 --> 16:22.340
Who do you mean by
comrades from over there?

16:24.040 --> 16:25.100
I don't know...

16:25.240 --> 16:26.230
What?

16:26.610 --> 16:30.780
The one that said we need to
protect this place was Mr. Misaki.

16:31.580 --> 16:35.640
I've trusted Mr. Misaki and just
kept on doing what he's told me to.

16:37.090 --> 16:40.620
Since the day he
passed away and left us...

16:40.790 --> 16:43.560
...I've been prepared
for a day like this.

16:46.970 --> 16:48.230
Sonezaki...

16:48.900 --> 16:52.200
Mr. Misaki let him outside.

16:52.270 --> 16:55.830
On the day we decided to
bring you guys here.

16:59.680 --> 17:03.980
I think Mr. Misaki
was seeing something.

17:04.820 --> 17:07.280
But I do not know what that is.

17:09.450 --> 17:11.390
He also did not tell me...

17:11.820 --> 17:15.320
...what was going to happen
when the barrier disappeared.

17:15.690 --> 17:18.560
Who are we up against?

17:18.960 --> 17:21.120
They have a significant amount of power.

17:21.470 --> 17:26.030
I heard that Mr. Misaki
went against them a long time ago.

17:26.640 --> 17:30.130
They came all of a sudden.

17:34.780 --> 17:37.250
What happened to those
that were taken away?

17:37.680 --> 17:41.880
They should have been released
somewhere, but I don't exactly know.

17:42.120 --> 17:43.490
You are irresponsible.

17:44.560 --> 17:48.290
I don't have any kind of power
to be able to save them.

17:49.460 --> 17:50.990
More importantly...

17:51.060 --> 17:53.050
...something bad is happening.

17:53.700 --> 17:54.760
Something bad?

17:55.270 --> 17:58.430
I'm confined in this place.

17:58.840 --> 18:01.470
If I try to leave, I will be killed.

18:03.140 --> 18:04.610
They're watching us.

18:05.380 --> 18:06.540
Three of them...

18:07.080 --> 18:10.880
They've been watching here
this whole time.

18:12.580 --> 18:13.450
Are you serious?

18:13.820 --> 18:14.980
They're strong.

18:15.150 --> 18:17.280
They're power is really strong.

18:17.360 --> 18:20.720
What's the point of confining me
in a place like this?

18:21.490 --> 18:25.330
Most of the humans that have obtained
authority and assets have been...

18:25.400 --> 18:27.730
...feeling somewhere
in their hearts that...

18:28.100 --> 18:33.470
...a form of power that you
cannot see exists in this world.

18:34.010 --> 18:36.910
And how they are
being moved by that power...

18:37.240 --> 18:42.080
Some of them call this luck and
others call this the power of god.

18:42.580 --> 18:46.410
Those that have found out about the
existence of the one you cannot see...

18:46.680 --> 18:51.750
...feel a premonition the world shall
start changing little by little from here.

18:53.060 --> 18:54.290
The reformation, huh?

18:54.690 --> 18:56.520
Everyone is scared...

18:56.760 --> 19:01.660
...of the fact that the value of everything
they have is going to be gone.

19:10.740 --> 19:15.410
There was a reason
Mr. Misaki chose this place.

19:16.050 --> 19:18.040
This is an energy spot.

19:18.550 --> 19:22.920
That's why Mr. Misaki was able
to make a complete barrier here.

19:23.190 --> 19:27.320
He was able to match his
consciousness to the wave frequency.

19:27.390 --> 19:28.420
Match his consciousness?

19:29.060 --> 19:33.000
It's something only those
with surpassed power can do.

19:33.330 --> 19:35.630
It's not something just anyone can do.

19:36.100 --> 19:38.190
But you two would be able to.

19:38.800 --> 19:40.100
We'd be able to?

19:40.910 --> 19:41.770
Yes.

19:41.970 --> 19:43.340
Come on, let's go.

19:43.410 --> 19:46.670
I thought you couldn't
leave this place?

19:47.250 --> 19:50.340
If it's with you two, I can.

19:50.820 --> 19:51.980
What do you mean?

19:52.050 --> 19:54.640
You take me and leave here.

19:55.150 --> 19:58.520
If we do such a thing,
then we must fight...

19:58.590 --> 20:00.850
That's his plan.

20:02.390 --> 20:04.330
They aren't that strong.

20:04.860 --> 20:08.860
They are trying so hard to
synchronize with the frequency, but...

20:08.930 --> 20:10.900
...they still haven't
been able to synchronize.

20:20.580 --> 20:21.570
Leave!

20:21.650 --> 20:23.010
You guys will leave!

20:23.080 --> 20:24.610
Leave Mikuriya here!

20:24.680 --> 20:26.650
If you do so...

20:26.720 --> 20:28.210
...we'll let you go.

20:28.290 --> 20:30.450
They're telling just us to leave.

20:30.590 --> 20:31.490
Let's go!

20:31.620 --> 20:34.390
Wait, you're taking me with you.

20:34.590 --> 20:36.990
You two are indebted to me.

20:37.060 --> 20:37.960
Indebted?

20:38.860 --> 20:39.960
You've got to be kidding me!

20:40.030 --> 20:43.970
I raised you two for 15 years.

20:44.540 --> 20:46.730
That's why you should help me.

20:46.800 --> 20:48.470
Don't order me!

20:49.340 --> 20:53.800
Regardless of the reason why you're
being confined here, I don't care!

20:55.450 --> 20:59.880
Have a taste of the feeling we had
when we were confined!

20:59.980 --> 21:04.220
The reason why you two
came here was not my decision.

21:04.290 --> 21:07.850
There was no other choice but
for you guys to be protected here.

21:07.930 --> 21:12.120
You two were born
along the flow like that.

21:12.200 --> 21:14.720
You used us as research material.

21:14.800 --> 21:19.670
I have also been looking for an
answer on where mankind is going.

21:19.970 --> 21:23.460
You two have
the power to help me.

21:23.780 --> 21:28.800
I want to leave Japan and spend the
rest of my life properly as a scholar.

21:29.280 --> 21:30.470
They are saying no!

21:30.750 --> 21:31.480
No!

21:31.550 --> 21:32.350
Leave!

21:32.420 --> 21:33.320
We'll kill you!

21:33.820 --> 21:35.580
You can do it!

21:35.650 --> 21:37.680
This is where you two grew up!

21:37.760 --> 21:40.720
You should be able to
synchronize with the frequency.

21:45.900 --> 21:46.890
Brother!

21:51.800 --> 21:52.860
Damn it.

21:53.870 --> 21:55.900
Mikuriya, this is farewell.

21:56.540 --> 21:59.510
Once we leave here,
we'll never see you again.

22:15.590 --> 22:17.080
They're saying to get out.

22:19.200 --> 22:20.530
It's a fight.

22:21.200 --> 22:22.060
Yeah.

22:31.240 --> 22:34.510
<i>An exact answer is nowhere.</i>

22:34.580 --> 22:37.170
<i>Even if you corner it, it still runs.</i>

22:37.250 --> 22:41.840
<i>It's that kind of repeating all the time.</i>

22:41.920 --> 22:45.150
<i>We hurt each other
and rip each other apart.</i>

22:45.220 --> 22:47.850
<i>We're complaining once again.</i>

22:47.930 --> 22:53.260
<i>When tomorrow comes, just like a lie,
you wear a mask and live on.</i>

22:53.330 --> 22:58.630
<i>I was wishing upon
the night stars...</i>

22:58.700 --> 23:03.970
<i>... for our distance
to become shorter.</i>

23:04.040 --> 23:10.680
<i>But if I try to bluff,
then I'm going to regret it.</i>

23:10.750 --> 23:13.220
<i>Words and feelings are reverse.</i>

23:13.280 --> 23:18.850
<i>Feelings that were asleep,
heart that was asleep, lure it out!</i>

23:18.920 --> 23:24.190
<i>Glamour that was asleep, myself
that was asleep, with your power!</i>

23:24.260 --> 23:29.720
<i>Please look at me quietly with the soul
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:29.800 --> 23:34.600
<i>I want you to go wilder inside me.</i>

23:34.670 --> 23:40.130
<i>Eyes that were asleep, emotions
that were asleep, wake them up!</i>

23:40.210 --> 23:45.480
<i>Memories that were asleep, dreams
that were asleep, with your power!</i>

23:45.550 --> 23:51.010
<i>Please melt me with the vision of kindness
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:51.090 --> 23:58.190
<i>I want to stay asleep
longer buried inside you.</i>

24:02.430 --> 24:05.870
This forest is a prison of
darkness that gouges out...

24:05.940 --> 24:07.700
...the fragile part of the heart.

24:08.040 --> 24:11.630
This forest is a purgatory of ice
where the sacrifices...

24:11.880 --> 24:13.610
...are contained within.

24:14.180 --> 24:17.310
The tunes of the battle
shred a severe melody...

24:18.020 --> 24:20.540
...as the will that is
faintly left in the forest...

24:20.620 --> 24:23.250
...opens up a door to another region.

24:24.090 --> 24:29.860
<i>Episode 15, "Surge"</i>

24:26.260 --> 24:29.390
Where are we headed?
